435,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Context: 'invokes third-party major tags'","AC1: 'Every third-party action in reconcile-bridge.yml is referenced by a full SHA'","reconcile-bridge.yml uses: actions/checkout@v7 (L103), actions/setup-python@v7 (L168), actions/cache@v6 (L184), aws-actions/configure-aws-credentials@v6 (L397)","tests/unit/test_release_workflow_pins.py test_all_uses_are_full_sha_pinned pins EVERY non-'./' uses: regardless of owner"],"finding":"The plan scopes the change to 'third-party' actions, but three of the four external references in reconcile-bridge.yml are GitHub-first-party (actions/checkout@v7, actions/setup-python@v7, actions/cache@v6) and only aws-actions/configure-aws-credentials@v6 is strictly third-party; the existing pin contract the plan extends (test_all_uses_are_full_sha_pinned) requires a full SHA on EVERY non-relative uses:, so a literal 'third-party only' implementation would leave the actions/* tags mutable and be inconsistent with (or fail) the contract it claims to extend.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f356ac53c67bd799c","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Acceptance Criteria (AC1) / Context","norm_id":"nc66b209a721f6249","priority":0.165,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer pins only aws-actions/* and leaves actions/checkout@v7 etc. on mutable tags, then the extended pin test (mirroring the every-uses regex) fails on actions/checkout@v7, or the workflow is left partially unpinned."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Reword Context/AC1 to 'every non-relative (external) action reference — GitHub-owned actions/* and third-party alike' and confirm the extended pin test applies the same all-`uses:` full-SHA rule used for release.yml.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na",